# Canonical Sources (Cursor ↔ Claude sync)

Use the same files in Cursor and Claude Code. Do not invent parallel conventions.

| Domain | Canonical file | Cursor behavior |
|--------|----------------|-----------------|
| Prose rules | `CLAUDE.md` | Always follow; wins on conflict |
| Style guide | `reference/style-guide.md` | Read before drafting or style review |
| Agent personas | `.claude/agents/*.md` | Read the matching file before acting in that role |
| Pipelines | `.claude/workflows/*.md` | Follow the workflow for the task type |
| Voice asymmetry repair | `.claude/skills/voice-asymmetry-fix/SKILL.md` | Read before pair-voice fixes |
| Character voice specs | `characters/*.md` `## Voice` | Read before any dialogue work |

## Conflict resolution

When an agent file disagrees with `CLAUDE.md`, **CLAUDE.md wins**. Example: agent files may mention em dashes; `CLAUDE.md` prohibits them.

## Cross-tool continuity

- Draft outputs go in `[book]/drafts/` with the same naming as workflows specify.
- Canonical chapter files: `[book]/chapter-[NN].md`
- Revision briefs: `[book]/drafts/chapter-[NN]-revision-brief.md`
- Plot changes in chapters require same-pass updates to `outline.md`, `plan.md`, and affected planning docs (Plot Sync Rule).
